==Enemy==
Unlike the original, this enemy's more of a low-ranged support unit with moderate health that can become threatening depending on what it appears with. Its damage isn't the highest, but proves to be annoying nonetheless with the 1.67s slow effect, especially coupled with the 75% [[Surge Attack#Mini-Surge|Mini-Surge]] chance that allows it to hit much further than it usually would. To round up its kit, it revives once with half health quickly. Its main weakness is its triple typing, which allows a large number of units to be effective against it, provided they could get within range.

==Strategy==
Thanks to its Mini-Surge and slow abilities, Angaburu can disrupt your line of meatshields to help the enemies it supports push faster, such as in [[Primeval Wood Area 17]], where Angaburu can slow your [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cats]] to a halt, thus leading to [[Winged Pigge]] wrecking havoc on your frontlines.

Killing Angaburu is not a hard task since it has three types that can be exploited. Using [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] with [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayers]] like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] will melt its health away.

In summary, Angaburu, like Henry, is really not that threatening, but when backed by other hard pushing enemies it will prove to be an annoying piece of support.

